--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -4,12 +4,26 @@ A small team notes app. Next.js App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind.
 
 ## Status
 
-- Users live in `src/lib/users.ts` as an in-memory list.
-- `/dashboard` shows the current user and the team.
-- There is no sign-in, no billing, and no email yet.
+- Auth is [Better Auth](https://better-auth.com): email + password and Google sign-in.
+- Users, sessions and accounts are stored in SQLite via Node's built-in `node:sqlite`
+  (file set by `DATABASE_PATH`). Tables are created/migrated on server start
+  (`src/instrumentation.ts`).
+- `src/lib/users.ts` reads users from that database; `getCurrentUser()` returns the
+  signed-in user and `requireUser()` redirects to `/sign-in` when there is none.
+- `/dashboard` is protected: `src/proxy.ts` redirects requests without a session
+  cookie, and the page itself verifies the session with `requireUser()`.
+- There is no billing and no email yet (so no email verification or password reset).
 
 ## Develop
 
+Requires Node 22.13+.
+
 ```bash
+cp .env.example .env.local   # then set BETTER_AUTH_SECRET (openssl rand -base64 32)
 npm run dev
 ```
+
+Google sign-in: create an OAuth client in Google Cloud Console, add
+`http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google` as an authorized redirect URI, and
+set `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` / `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`. The "Continue with Google" button
+only appears when both are set.
